ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckCloakCapFormal = captain's formal cloak
    .desc = A lavish and decorated cloak for special occasions.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckMantleMiningBlood = bloody miner's mantle
    .desc = A miner's mantle covered in the blood of enemies.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckGeneralFormalCloak = general's formal cloak
    .desc = A lavish black cloak with gold trim, worn only on special occasions.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingAdmiralShoulder = captain-admiral's cloak
    .desc = A massive blue cloak with gold trim. It is presented to captains who have been through a lot...
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckDarkCloakVClose = dark cloak
    .desc = A long, loose garment the color of night that flows elegantly around the figure, adding an air of mystery.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingHeadDarkHoodV = dark cloak hood
    .desc = Deep and soft as a shadow, it frames the face with a sense of cozy mystery. It perfectly complements the cloak, giving its wearer the look of a mysterious wanderer.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckMantleMining = miner's mantle
    .desc = Looks like you just tore down a cargo banner and put it on.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckMantleCE = chief engineer's manica
    .desc = Segmented orange pieces covering the shoulders and arms of an experienced chief engineer. They signify the hazards of the job and the dangers faced to earn it.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckCloakFugitiveCloak = monochrome cloak
    .desc = A black cloak with white crosses and a fluffy white collar. It's a federal crime, buster.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckCloakGoldenCentComm = gilded CentCom cloak
    .desc = A luxurious gold-gilded cloak worn by the highest-ranking officials.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckAngelWings = angel wings
    .desc = Snow-white angel wings. I can be your angel...
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckMimeMantleOffShoulder = mime's off-shoulder mantle
    .desc = A black-and-white striped mantle made for mimes, worn off the shoulders.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckCloakHop = head of personnel's cloak
    .desc = A blue cloak with red shoulders and gold buttons, proving you are the gatekeeper to any airlock on the station.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckCloakHos = head of security's cloak
    .desc = An exquisite dark and red cloak fitting for those who can assert dominance over wrongdoers. Take a stab at being civil in prosecution.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckPocscloak2 = black officer's cloak
    .desc = A heavy black cloak with gold studs along the edges and a gold emblem on the back. It makes any officer look like the one in charge.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckHosRobe = head of security's decadent robe
    .desc = A comfy formal robe in deep red with gold epaulettes, given to veteran heads of security.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckCloakCapFormalImp = captain's navy formal cloak
    .desc = A lavish dark navy cloak with gold trim for special occasions.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckBronzeCross = bronze cross
    .desc = A cross cast from bronze, hung on a beaded cord. Grandma would surely have pressed it to your bruises.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingCloakCmo = chief medical officer's cloak
    .desc = A sterile blue cloak with a green cross, radiating with a sense of duty and willingness to help others.
ent-SunriseSponsorClothingNeckMantleBlueshield = blueshield officer mantle
    .desc = A dark blue mantle with gold trim. Cut so as not to get in the way of a bodyguard's work.
